{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire","id":1394467,"title":"After Adventure, what's our desire.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-05T18:16:37-07:00","id":1394467,"title":"After Adventure, what's our desire.","content":"What it says on the tin. Both Amina and Adventure are in the writing pipeline at various stages. So, what kind of stuff do we want next?<br /> <br /> In terms of games I'd like a far future setting with aliens, supertech, and new ways of handling the major powers.<br /> <br /> I'd also like a time war game where the dials could be moved around freely from Fritz Lieber's &quot;Big Time&quot;, to Tommy Tomorrow and the Time patrol, to &quot;Doctor Who&quot;, as the players wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T18:46:48-07:00","id":1394470,"title":"","content":"Both. Everything. <br /> <br /> Though on a serious note I think the time travel one sounds really interesting. For many reasons but one of them being the whole unstuck in time thing of Mercer, meaning said setting already has a potential character in it that could be used as a sort of spring board towards adventure. Like imagine if due to his own special nature Matt Mercer created a version of Aeon that is basically everywhere, like how the Impossible Girl is in all places and times so is Aeon. <br /> <br /> The other major period is long long ago, a sort of ancient world with some mythical non-mythical (because Trinity isn't about 'magic') elements to it. That would also be an intriguing area to cover in a way that is not really being covered. <br /> <br /> Though your mention f the far future is also great. The idea of less the early phase of humans into space and more say how Star Wars is in a mature galaxy with over 25k worth of history would be brilliant. Or maybe something like the Foundation Galaxy of Asimov, just with aliens. Or... Basically a mature spacefaring society with a place for Inspired, Novas, and Psiads. <br /> <br /> I will say this one of the things that I would really like for TC to give us is 'rules' for a more 'fantasy' like setting. Its done scifi and pulp and so to have fantasy be written up using its system would be like a perfect blend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T19:48:05-07:00","id":1394486,"title":"","content":"We have Aegis as a future announcement, so the mythic non-mystical setting is somewhere in the line.<br /> <br /> My favorite idea is a far future setting with balanced Novas and powerful Psiads exploring the universe (or even multiverse).<br /> <br /> But the time travelers are very interesting...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T01:15:00-07:00","id":1394519,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d definitely like to see Aegis (the long ago proposed setting) be moved to the head of the queue.<br /> <br /> I could also see a Victorian era (late 1800s) or classic sci-fi (1950s) era being fun, but they might overlap with Adventure! too much. And I kinda feel like the core does a fine job at covering the \u201cSuper Spy\u201d era of the 60s and 70s as is, so maybe a softcover with setting info/adventure hooks/period specific gifts from that period might be useful, but I\u2019m not sure it warrants a full blown era.<br /> <br /> Hmmm.... Actually that could be kinda neat. Doing supplementary \u201cminor eras\u201d that are \u201ctoo close\u201d to the Main Eras to warrant full hardcovers with tons of new rules, but where enough has changed that some additional info might be useful to help fit into an alternate genre or simply some advice on how the world was at the time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thinking on it, I suppose I\u2019m most interested in what this universe was like before the Hammersmith experiment and the Aeon society. I mean, it\u2019s still not gonna be entirely normal at those points, but without a kickstart from something to increase the weirdness level, it seems like Talents are the only ones who get much play and they\u2019re intentionally subtle, so... I guess I\u2019m curious what other periods of increased weirdness have occurred in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> A time travel focused \u201cmeta-era\u201d could be cool, but I kinda feel like we need more era books to exist first before that one would be very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T01:19:03-07:00","id":1394521,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Given the work Onyx Path has already done with the Dark Eras books for the Chronicles of Darkness, it might be worth poking through them for periods in history that might fit well in the Trinity Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T01:53:25-07:00","id":1394525,"title":"","content":"I do like the Aegis idea. I had, at one point, wanted to design a game similar to the concept of it. <br /> I do not think that time traveler would be a good option along the main continuum but I would certainly love to see a Slider-esque game. You pop into unique timelines wherein the universe is changed in subtle ways. Be it that WW 2 ended differently or if Communism never took hold or if the Library of Alexandria was saved and so forth and so on. That would be, to me, an awesome idea. Perhaps mix in things like time travel with these alternate timelines?<br /> You have an overarching organization. Their world collapsed due to too much interference in time travel. So now, they go to other timelines and nudge something here or there to basically chrono-form a world to what they had before they messed things up. The players can either explore these worlds or else try to go back and fix what the bad guys changed. This could fold the alternate timeline back into the main one and deny the bad guys an option.<br /> Y'know what? If OPP does not make this, I just may. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T04:27:22-07:00","id":1394536,"title":"","content":"The Slider idea is great, and could be something for Talents using Talents Powered Science Items. We have one example in Media Res, it\u2019s not difficult to expand over it, maybe just let the characters invent things like that items.<br /> <br /> I would buy it on the Nexus...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T05:10:46-07:00","id":1394543,"title":"","content":"I'm with BrilliantRain on the idea of doing something like the Dark Eras books with the Trinityverse. Once you've got the main eras set out and time travel set up and/or limited both themes (Super Spy, Steampunk, Classic Sci-fi) and alternates outside of the timeline (basically any alternative history plus how to cross actual magic into the setting) can be accommodated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-08-2020, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T06:20:06-07:00","id":1394551,"title":"","content":"On the \u201cactual magic\u201d part, I have would suggest to keep it inside the 3 sources (Flux, Quantum and Psi).<br /> <br /> Starting with Psi, we can have magic users that have general powers, like a witch that can change shape, a zombi master that can control people bodies, a fire mage and things like that. It\u2019s a matter of picking a Psiad with the proper Modes and combinations.<br /> <br /> Quantum can work from guys that are above human condition (on a Stalwart level) to a god (on Nova level). Maybe you can have a bunch of Stalwarts using super tech devices to work as demigods, or a kind of Quantum user that can control the elements on a limited way (Novas a the end of Quantum users scale, we could have a more balanced one that can still control the quantum forces out of their bodies).<br /> <br /> Flux can be used to subtle changing reality, time travel, dimensional travel, Summoning creatures from other dimensions (Aberrants in the form of demons or angels if you prefere).<br /> I am working on a way to add this effects to TC, other than Fists of Flux (I don\u2019t know if I just expand on it or if I make an entire book with the same Tier III Talent concept), the idea is to bring some of the dark magic feeling (on the Cthulu-esque style) to the setting, with cultists capable of summoning bizarre monsters from other dimensions thru long rituals (more mundane level magic), Talents capable of conscious dramatic editing and Excelsiors capable of reality bending effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:16:04-07:00","id":1394553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1394551#post1394551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the \u201cactual magic\u201d part, I have would suggest to keep it inside the 3 sources (Flux, Quantum and Psi).<br /> <br /> Starting with Psi, we can have magic users that have general powers, like a witch that can change shape, a zombi master that can control people bodies, a fire mage and things like that. It\u2019s a matter of picking a Psiad with the proper Modes and combinations.<br /> <br /> Quantum can work from guys that are above human condition (on a Stalwart level) to a god (on Nova level). Maybe you can have a bunch of Stalwarts using super tech devices to work as demigods, or a kind of Quantum user that can control the elements on a limited way (Novas a the end of Quantum users scale, we could have a more balanced one that can still control the quantum forces out of their bodies).<br /> <br /> Flux can be used to subtle changing reality, time travel, dimensional travel, Summoning creatures from other dimensions (Aberrants in the form of demons or angels if you prefere).<br /> I am working on a way to add this effects to TC, other than Fists of Flux (I don\u2019t know if I just expand on it or if I make an entire book with the same Tier III Talent concept), the idea is to bring some of the dark magic feeling (on the Cthulu-esque style) to the setting, with cultists capable of summoning bizarre monsters from other dimensions thru long rituals (more mundane level magic), Talents capable of conscious dramatic editing and Excelsiors capable of reality bending effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good for in the main continuity magic, and how the setting should go. I was talking about out of continuity and out of left field stuff. No core supplement should use actual magic, however when you're setting up something twisted and silly, such rules are useful. Heck, just take the version of Mage magic they used in a supplement for Hunter: the Reckoning polish the rough edges and put it in an appendix in the back of a toolkit book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T07:22:51-07:00","id":1394557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1394553#post1394553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's good for in the main continuity magic, and how the setting should go. I was talking about out of continuity and out of left field stuff. No core supplement should use actual magic, however when you're setting up something twisted and silly, such rules are useful. Heck, just take the version of Mage magic they used in a supplement for Hunter: the Reckoning polish the rough edges and put it in an appendix in the back of a toolkit book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea, sounds fun and playable.<br /> <br /> I was playing with the idea of Ars Magica for Storypath, but it\u2019s far from silly and fun, it\u2019s more methodical and mechanical... I like it, but it is not for everyone...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 06-06-2020, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T09:00:34-07:00","id":1394571,"title":"","content":"Aegis. Time travel. Space opera. Like a League of Extraordinary Gentlemen clone. I personally would love to see the Three Musketeers era for TC (Milady de Winter is the ancestor of the King of the World and I really admire Milady as a villain) but idk how popular that would be.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> I Liked your idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T15:02:48-07:00","id":1394636,"title":"","content":"I think I would like some rules for interaction between the various eras. I strongly suspect that time and realm travel will be a thing in the continuum at some point since the various setting books all share a core. Of particular interest to me is making psions and novas (or aberrants if you prefer) work alongside one another. I think it would be awesome to run something like what occurs in the Fate of Humanity bit in Chapter 11 of the Aeon book. As they say its a different era. That sounds like a cool if short setting book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:10:55-07:00","id":1394650,"title":"","content":"Honestly I would wait for Adventure rules before anything, but putting all kinds of character together is the thing I really any to with TC.<br /> <br /> When I saw Dimension invaders in Media Res it become a thing I really want to happen officially (meanwhile I will use my little rules for tier III Talents).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T16:22:51-07:00","id":1394652,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1580\" data-vbnamecard=\"1580\">andrewm9</a> that\u2019s a really good idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T17:17:21-07:00","id":1394667,"title":"","content":"So, I kind of want something that should probably be a supplement for Anima. Because what I've read on Anima seems like it's gonna be Cyberpunk BUT focus mostly on the hacking, online, netrunneresq side of things.<br /> <br /> I want a cyberpunk supplement that focuses on tier 2 character cyborgs. William Gibson style hard-tech augmented humans who could go toe to toe with Psions or low-end Novas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T18:21:09-07:00","id":1394685,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar509_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"509\" data-vbnamecard=\"509\">TiwazTyrsfist</a> also a cool idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T20:42:26-07:00","id":1394710,"title":"","content":"If the rules change after Adventure! comes out, I really want to try making 1970s Adventure! for the Nexis. <br /> <br /> As far as official settings, I think it would be kind of cool to have something set before recorded history (Antediluvian or something) that is some sort of lost &quot;high fantasy&quot; epoch of Psionic (or other Flux-based) super science, interplanetary/interdimensional travel, and other over the top craziness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T05:23:43-07:00","id":1394759,"title":"","content":"I think at this point the focus should be on expanding the settings we have. Pushing out rather than pushing forward, so to speak. I'd love something equivalent to a Night Horrors book for Trinity that gives us info on potential antagonists in the form of organizations and whatnot. Just more stuff that goes into some of the nitty gritty aspects of the settings and provides story seeds to follow. So material that could give you some deeper story hooks for if you want to run a more social type of game, for example. The main boon of the ready-made Aeon characters were the story seeds the book provided. Having not just a paragraph of inspiration but a clear, brief outline of &quot;this is what you can do, where you can start, some stuff you need to get past, and here's how it might end and where you can go from there&quot; was incredibly helpful.<br /> <br /> I feel like Trinity is built to not just allow but encourage so many possible kinds of campaign in a way a lot of settings aren't necessarily. Like any good RPG setting is going to allow you the opportunity to engage in any kind of adventure you want, but usually they give a fairly clear default and don't go out of their way to suggest alternatives. Trinity is all about offering up alternatives and there isn't that same assumed default state of play. I think supplements that help players and storyguides get their heads around all the potential that the settings offer would really be a great leap forward in helping players deal with all the possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T16:22:20-07:00","id":1394866,"title":"","content":"I'd enjoy seeing some sort of &quot;hidden worlds&quot; book for Adventure!. Something covering the Hollow Earth, forgotten plateaus, lost cities, underground catacombs, monster islands, and even the Moon, Mars and Venus as envisioned by 19th and early 20th century fiction.<br /> <br /> Some sort of media/celebrity handbook for Aberrant would be cool also. Maybe a corporate/business one too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:24:35-07:00","id":1394895,"title":"","content":"I love the Adventure! Hidden Worlds idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:27:38-07:00","id":1394899,"title":"","content":"Let us now both tend our gardens...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> Voltaire, Candide. I said this to my bff after our last big fight. She didn\u2019t know the allusion but she agreed with the sentiment. Your sig (the quote from Voltaire\u2019s Tolerance) reminded me of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T17:43:03-07:00","id":1394910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1394866#post1394866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd enjoy seeing some sort of &quot;hidden worlds&quot; book for Adventure!. Something covering the Hollow Earth, forgotten plateaus, lost cities, underground catacombs, monster islands, and even the Moon, Mars and Venus as envisioned by 19th and early 20th century fiction.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like Penelope, I second this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T19:19:50-07:00","id":1394934,"title":"","content":"Make us 3. Super science rocket on the best Jules Verne style, exploring exotic planets, or climbing down a Vulcan to find the center of the earth.<br /> <br /> I will have to take a look on my Jules Verne books, and in Candide (the optimism) after a few decades...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T20:40:25-07:00","id":1394976,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz definitely. The hidden worlds were one of my favorite parts when I read Adventure! 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T22:53:22-07:00","id":1395008,"title":"","content":"Ian Watson, if you\u2019re reading this thread, please put \u201cHidden Worlds\u201d on the list of possible stretch goals for the Adventure! KS.<br /> <br /> (assuming it\u2019s not already there anyway)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:35:54-07:00","id":1395029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1394866#post1394866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd enjoy seeing some sort of &quot;hidden worlds&quot; book for Adventure!. Something covering the Hollow Earth, forgotten plateaus, lost cities, underground catacombs, monster islands, and even the Moon, Mars and Venus as envisioned by 19th and early 20th century fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fifth supporter of this supplement book! <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a>, if you really want ot be heard - just tag the user. For greater good of <b>Adventure!</b> gameline, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> - please consider this <b>Hidden Worlds</b> as Kickstarter Streach Goal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I always loved Atlantis, Mu, Lemura and similar stuff! ( Runed <b>Mage the Awakening</b> by 12 years on Atlantis alone, trying to implant Atlantean Pantheon to modern <b>Scion</b> game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> / Yes, I waiting for the <b>Scion Companion</b> to read on this one! / )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-08-2020, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T05:53:15-07:00","id":1395064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1395008#post1395008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ian Watson, if you\u2019re reading this thread, please put \u201cHidden Worlds\u201d on the list of possible stretch goals for the Adventure! KS.<br /> <br /> (assuming it\u2019s not already there anyway)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say put it on the list of planned Adventure! supplements (cf. Distant Worlds, Under Alien Suns and Terra Firma, none of which were Aeon/corebook KS stretch goals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T09:28:23-07:00","id":1395088,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Hidden Worlds, I would actually love if for the Core there could eventually be something expanding on Flux and the interdimensional side of that. With Talents being the main Core splat, science fiction is kind of important to the world-building, but it doesn't get touched on much. I'd love a supplement talking about Flux and general weird science themes and how to integrate them into your campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T09:58:38-07:00","id":1395096,"title":"","content":"Core by itself is a great game, it do work fine (while Scion Origin don\u2019t do great by it self). But yes, it misses a more complete setting exploring Talents in the world. I think we will see more about hard science fiction in Anima, and more on Flux and Interdimensional things in Adventure!, but I would love a more complete setting for Core in modern days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T11:24:20-07:00","id":1395111,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a Trinity Continuum Players Guide/Companion that expands on a lot of the stuff in the core book and fleshes out the modern setting a bit more, including a discussion of different genres that TC can cover. <br /> <br /> <br /> As for a Hidden Worlds type book, in my ideal world, I'd like to see such a book cover at least some of the following.<ul><li>Under Your Nose and Out of the Way: The sort of hidden stuff lurking behind the everyday world of the 1930s, including but not limited to various hidden lairs and secret locations (the equivalents to Doc Savage's skyscraper headquarters, the Shadow's Sanctum, Miskatonic University's library, secret labs, &quot;Lost&quot; subway/underground tube stations, etc.). Probably also some mention of things like Stonehenge, the catacombs under Paris (including the special area under the opera house), various private clubs, &quot;haunted&quot; houses, and the like.</li> <li>Lost Cities and Islands: The secret ape city from the original book, the mythical city of Shambalah, the hidden high tech industrial Metropolis, the lost Roman colony in Africa or South America, Skull Island, the stuff from H. Rider Haggard's novels, the place where a mad scientist is trying to turn animals into people, plateaus or canyons with hidden dinosaurs, lost tribes, the headquarters of the secret society of assassins, weird stuff buried under the ice of Antarctica, and all that fun stuff.</li> <li>Under the Sea: besides rules/guidelines for deep sea diving and submarines, including super high tech ones, ship wrecks and lost treasures, lost Atlantis and other possible sunken cities, the Deep Ones, and probably rules for aquatic Stalwart types along the lines of Namor/Aquaman or mermaids.</li> <li>Out of This World: Leaving the planet in the 1930s, including rules/guidelines for jet planes and rocket ships, and probably Stargates and the like as well. The Moon, Mars, and Venus as envisioned by the science fiction and science fantasy of the 1930s and earlier, including alien races. This may also include Mercury and the hypothetical planet Vulcan. Also Counter-Earth, the world that shares our orbit but is always on the other side of the sun. And probably alternate dimensions, including one resembling Flash Gordon.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T11:40:22-07:00","id":1395114,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7372_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7372\" data-vbnamecard=\"7372\">Lady Gray</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> those are all really great ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T16:01:40-07:00","id":1395473,"title":"","content":"I'd also love a Far future Space Opera setting. Something 100+ years past \u00c6on.<br /> <br /> Inspiration: Star Trek, Orville, Sol Bianca, Outlaw Star, Angel Links, etc.<br /> <br /> Something where the default play mode is (or at least can be) episodic space travel, new planet of the week sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T17:01:33-07:00","id":1395480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1395473#post1395473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also love a Far future Space Opera setting. Something 100+ years past \u00c6on.<br /> <br /> Inspiration: Star Trek, Orville, Sol Bianca, Outlaw Star, Angel Links, etc.<br /> <br /> Something where the default play mode is (or at least can be) episodic space travel, new planet of the week sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sindbad in the stars, always fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T14:14:51-07:00","id":1395674,"title":"","content":"My favorite Sci-Fi trope is Lost Technology. Any stuff where a long dead race left behind stuff way in advance of the current interstellar society's ability to understand or duplicate. That's something I want to see more of in \u00c6on and post-\u00c6on games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T18:07:44-07:00","id":1395711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1395674#post1395674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite Sci-Fi trope is Lost Technology. Any stuff where a long dead race left behind stuff way in advance of the current interstellar society's ability to understand or duplicate. That's something I want to see more of in \u00c6on and post-\u00c6on games.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s at least a few of those in Distant Worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:19:27-07:00","id":1395724,"title":"","content":"I'd love a Renaissance/Early Modern Swashbuckler setting (it would mix the various types from First Edition Adventure! but in their 2e forms.) I'd go with the name Anthor ( an Alchemist's furnace).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T19:27:28-07:00","id":1395728,"title":"","content":"I was watching Cloverfield Paradox the other they, and the idea of the space station with a generator using interdimensional energy (that shifts the entire station to another reality and change the timeline of multiple universes) is interesting. Maybe it\u2019s a new version of the Hammersmith teluric engine...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T12:05:22-07:00","id":1396053,"title":"","content":"I kind of want one of those &quot;modern people get transported to the past and start implementing new tech and ideas&quot; settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T13:58:41-07:00","id":1396070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1396053#post1396053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of want one of those &quot;modern people get transported to the past and start implementing new tech and ideas&quot; settings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Yes. YES!!! So much this. Sooooooo much this. Sooooo very much. <br /> <br /> I don't know how exactly such implementation would work since there is a lot of nuances to bringing tech and such but I so very much want a game like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T15:44:15-07:00","id":1396079,"title":"","content":"Like Eric Flint and the 1632 series","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T20:15:34-07:00","id":1396103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1396079#post1396079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Eric Flint and the 1632 series</div> </div> </div> </div>That, L. Sprague de Camp's Lest Darkness Fall (one of the originators of the idea), David Drake and Eric Flint's Belisarius series, John Birmingham's Axis of Time series, Harry Turtledove's Guns of the South, and SM Stirling's Island in the Sea of Time. <br /> <br /> The two biggest questions/issues for such a thing is &quot;who/what goes back&quot; and &quot;to when?&quot; The first indicates what they know and can do, what resources they have, as well as - perhaps most important - what are they hoping to accomplish? A small town vs. a US carrier fleet vs a single person. And the second indicates what &quot;current&quot; resources they have to work with, what the cultural barriers will be, and what can actually be changed. <br /> <br /> If I were writing such a thing as fiction, I'd likely opt for Wessex during the reign of Alfred the Great and the viking invasions, or the United States sometime between 1750 and 1780, but mainly because of specific things I'd want to do with the story. As a RPG setting, it's harder to say. Maybe the first century BC, with rival factions having been thrown back into the Roman Republic, the Han dynasty, and maybe Parthian Persian and Satavahana India as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:42:53-07:00","id":1396284,"title":"","content":"It also occurs to me that Trinity Continuum might be a good system for some sort of &quot;Adventures Across Alternate Earths&quot; set up, where the PCs are agents of some sort of pan-dimensional force protecting it from various threats. GURPS already does something similar with its Infinite Worlds setting, but I think TC would be a little less rules heavy, and would enable me do to something that's kind of a mash up of Sliders (if it had been smarter and not consistently gone for some of the dumbest alternate worlds possible), the Jet Li movie The One, and some of the better aspects of Star Trek. Maybe a United Federation of Worlds that includes a &quot;one year from tomorrow&quot; version of ours, an Earth-Beta that's just like ours save for a huge number of minor differences (such as BETA winning the home video format wars of the 80s, giving it its name), a world where Britain never got involved in WW1 and Germany won, a world where India became the dominant global cultural power instead of Europe, a world of sentient dinosaur people, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:04:17-07:00","id":1405993,"title":"","content":"One good idea for a one off book might take the trope of the &quot;Lost Colony&quot; and blend in the idea of being timelost. Have the castaways from a badly lost colony ship surviving on a distant planet. Civilization collapsed because of irresolvable struggles among the castaways, who were never meant to go to the same world. <br /> <br /> But people are rebuilding society. They are relearning ancient skills and technologies. Rediscovering who and what they are. I'd prefer the PCs to be like the PCs from 1e Adventure! I'd add in some extra Knacks like a Mind speach ability for each basic type. The Mesmerist knack should be the most flexible. But each form of the knack should allow easy two-way communication. Even between those that don't share a language.<br /> <br /> I see the setting as Planetary Romance with extra helpings of Swashbuckling and Gold Age Sci Fi paradigm breakthroughs.<br /> <br /> As I said I see this as a one off.<br /> <br /> It might be called &quot;Ascending!'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:28:27-07:00","id":1406000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1405993#post1405993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One good idea for a one off book might take the trope of the &quot;Lost Colony&quot; and blend in the idea of being timelost. Have the castaways from a badly lost colony ship surviving on a distant planet. Civilization collapsed because of irresolvable struggles among the castaways, who were never meant to go to the same world.<br /> <br /> But people are rebuilding society. They are relearning ancient skills and technologies. Rediscovering who and what they are. I'd prefer the PCs to be like the PCs from 1e Adventure! I'd add in some extra Knacks like a Mind speach ability for each basic type. The Mesmerist knack should be the most flexible. But each form of the knack should allow easy two-way communication. Even between those that don't share a language.<br /> <br /> I see the setting as Planetary Romance with extra helpings of Swashbuckling and Gold Age Sci Fi paradigm breakthroughs.<br /> <br /> As I said I see this as a one off.<br /> <br /> It might be called &quot;Ascending!'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This idea doesn't just get a like from me it gets a quote because I LOVE IT!!! I think a Planetary Romance slash Lost Colony slash Timelost campaign setting story arc would be absolutely brilliant. There are so many potentials for this depending on what power sources one would want in such a campaign. I mean the version with the Inspired is different from one with Psiads/Psions is differnet from one with Novas is different from one with all the groups in various portions. Where they are would also change the idea - a lost planet in the present is different from another dimension is different from the castaways waking up on Earth a few million years ago. I would totally support and sponsor and buy the heck out of this. <br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> Another idea that I would love to see done using the Storypath based rules is a sort of Nation Building slash Kingdom Ruling slash Noble House Operating game. (Scifi could be like Dune, fantasy could be like ASOIAF) The players would play as the leaders of the ruling organization of the nation/kingdom/house. I would love to see this done using this system because I think there is a lot of potential enhancement when one considers powers and Gifts and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T14:50:11-07:00","id":1406002,"title":"","content":"Honestly my favorite \u201cother point in timeline\u201d is Aegis. Playing a super powered human (even if just a bit above regular) in a time before civilization (there were civilizations but not around where the chars are) would be really interesting.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the idea of a lost spaceship finding different planets every week while looking for a way home may be interesting. Not worth a setting, but I may write a CC about that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T15:38:35-07:00","id":1406012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1405993#post1405993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One good idea for a one off book might take the trope of the &amp;quot;Lost Colony&amp;quot; and blend in the idea of being timelost. Have the castaways from a badly lost colony ship surviving on a distant planet. Civilization collapsed because of irresolvable struggles among the castaways, who were never meant to go to the same world. <br /> <br /> But people are rebuilding society. They are relearning ancient skills and technologies. Rediscovering who and what they are. I'd prefer the PCs to be like the PCs from 1e Adventure! I'd add in some extra Knacks like a Mind speach ability for each basic type. The Mesmerist knack should be the most flexible. But each form of the knack should allow easy two-way communication. Even between those that don't share a language.<br /> <br /> I see the setting as Planetary Romance with extra helpings of Swashbuckling and Gold Age Sci Fi paradigm breakthroughs.<br /> <br /> As I said I see this as a one off.<br /> <br /> It might be called &amp;quot;Ascending!'</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds really cool based on the setting description, but I wouldn\u2019t mind some more details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T19:12:17-07:00","id":1406037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406012#post1406012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds really cool based on the setting description, but I wouldn\u2019t mind some more details.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A few things to help...<br /> <br /> 1) The ship that misjumped went through a realm of flux and came out about 30,000 light-years from Earth and in or close to the year 16,000 BCE.<br /> <br /> 2) Most of the passengers and crew were in stasis cells for two thousand years for the ship to terraform the planet with their limited resources. The world has a full eco-system, but one where many animals have been touched/mutated by flux. This world has dragons, griffins, and unicorns, as well as stranger beasts.<br /> <br /> 3) The passengers were from multiple different Earth cultures that don't actually respect each other. Example: The North Americans that were on the ship were Social Democrats seeking to restore American democracy in an interstellar colony. They were generally assumed to be agents of the FSA there to disrupt and destroy. They were always treated as outcasts. The colonists were culturally incompatible and deeply hostile to each other. Their society collapsed because of bigotry, anger, and paranoia. Chauvinistic worldviews dominate this world and limit communication.<br /> <br /> 4) This is a highly maritime world, there is slightly more land area relative to ocean area than planet Earth, But this landmass is scattered in islands and small continents. No landmass is more than three-fourths the size of Australia, landmasses as large as Britain aren't common.<br /> <br /> The climate is more moderate than Earth because it is more maritime than Earth. There are ice caps and the deep oceans are oxygenated.<br /> <br /> 5) No society has achieved industrialization. However, there are enclaves where technology is more advanced, these generally have a good source of electrical power, most are linked hydro-power dams. These rarely have better than mid-20th century technology. However, some do better. Most of these sites are universities and teaching hospitals. All of these are archives.<br /> <br /> More later....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T19:44:05-07:00","id":1406040,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I remember Mystara post Blackmore fall. Blackmore was high technological / technomantic society that suffered a huge accident that destroyed the capital and broke the entire civilization, taking the general tech level to somewhere around Iron Age, with some left over technology that is treated as magical artifacts. In fact the technology is very much magical, but yet technological, with robots, laser guns and things like that.<br /> <br /> Well, that is pretty much what I remember, as in the last 20 years all that I read on Mystara was basically centred in the Immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:22:34-07:00","id":1406092,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> cool \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz I love Mystara! Bought a ton of old Mystara stuff on DTRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T06:35:17-07:00","id":1406101,"title":"","content":"Mystara is my favorite D&amp;D setting. So many things to do, so many options, it\u2019s a crazy setting.<br /> <br /> First, I was thinking about running a Scion campaign in Mystara, but TC may fit much better!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:19:37-07:00","id":1406167,"title":"","content":"I think making Mystara a TC alternate Earth (or maybe a distant planet) is a great idea. What do you think about the Hollow World?<br /> <br /> Sorry. This might be getting a little off track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:51:58-07:00","id":1406179,"title":"","content":"It fits very well on the TC as an alternate Earth. I would say it fits better than in Scion and Even in D&amp;D (while its fantasy, it\u2019s too out of the box to fit properly). Of course it requires a few changes, like Immortals (what would be Novas equivalents) can evolve from anyone, even magicians (Psiad equivalents) and heroes (Talents equivalents), but other than that I think it fits nicely.<br /> <br /> Hollow World is one of the things I would never remove for several reasons, first of all it\u2019s a monstrous adventure hook. It also fits on that SyFy show, Sanctuary. That show is an interesting cross to Adventure!<br /> <br /> Edit: mixed the show name! Is sanctuary, with Lt Carter as Helen \u201cImmortal\u201d Magnus","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-03-2020, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T17:34:16-07:00","id":1406188,"title":"","content":"I want, and nearly wrote up a pitch for, a Trinity Continuum: Western game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T07:59:02-07:00","id":1406273,"title":"","content":"I like the western idea. Back during 1e I ran a game set in the 1890's that was loosly based on The Adventures of Briscoe County Jr. It was fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T18:21:35-07:00","id":1406361,"title":"","content":"The Victorian Period in England, the Old West, and the Meji Restoration all happed over roughly the same time period. It could certainly be a fun period for Trinity Continuum play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T10:51:24-07:00","id":1406467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a Trinity Continuum: Western game. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a game set in the 1890's that was loosly based on The Adventures of Briscoe County Jr. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Victorian Period in England, the Old West, and the Meji Restoration </div> </div> </div>But that's just Adventure (or the Core even) with some setting restrictions.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can put out a &quot;Dark Eras&quot; type book for eras where only minor rule/theme adjustments are needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 08-05-2020, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T11:33:10-07:00","id":1406473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406467#post1406467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But that's just Adventure (or the Core even) with some setting restrictions.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can put out a &quot;Dark Eras&quot; type book for eras where only minor rule/theme adjustments are needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not wrong, there was an Old West cowboy, and a cantankerous one in the Adventure! Core Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-18-2023, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T19:20:35-07:00","id":1406553,"title":"","content":"I want tier 3 talents, and cyborgs. I would also like to see a far future setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T19:35:59-07:00","id":1406559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406553#post1406553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want tier 3 talents, and cyborgs. I would also like to see a far future setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cyborgs we will see in Anima.<br /> <br /> Tier 3 Talents are not officially in any book, but you can take a look in my take on them, it\u2019s on my signature.<br /> <br /> When you say far future you mean like Foundation and Dune or not so far future? I would like to see something like the Foundation for TC, then the Doyen were defeated a long time ago and humanity start building an interstellar empire/league of worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T20:39:54-07:00","id":1406572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406559#post1406559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cyborgs we will see in Anima.<br /> <br /> Tier 3 Talents are not officially in any book, but you can take a look in my take on them, it\u2019s on my signature.<br /> <br /> When you say far future you mean like Foundation and Dune or not so far future? I would like to see something like the Foundation for TC, then the Doyen were defeated a long time ago and humanity start building an interstellar empire/league of worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna second the idea of Foundation for Trinity so hard. Honestly, the very nature of Trinity makes playing as a member of either the First or Second Foundation a perfect fit. Even more it fits in the whole Hope nature of the gameline as the Foundation is all about trying to bring about a good, glorious future. <br /> <br /> Also, a Dune like game would be awesome too. Space Feudalism with intrigue and the game of noble houses and adventure galore would be amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T01:47:56-07:00","id":1406597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406467#post1406467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's just Adventure (or the Core even) with some setting restrictions.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can put out a &quot;Dark Eras&quot; type book for eras where only minor rule/theme adjustments are needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I look so much for the <b>Adventure! </b>corebook, now! \u2764\ufe0f This game seems to be everything I need to do Trinity games in the past I would like to run. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T02:10:36-07:00","id":1406599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406559#post1406559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When you say far future you mean like Foundation and Dune or not so far future? I would like to see something like the Foundation for TC, then the Doyen were defeated a long time ago and humanity start building an interstellar empire/league of worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like books with both flavors. Although the really far future one think more Book of the New Sun. Dune is roughly twenty-four thousand years in the future, BotNS is at least 100,000 years on and probably much more. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile the nearer one could be played like Star Trek, Northwest Smith, whole bunches of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T22:06:46-07:00","id":1406727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1394467-after-adventure-what-s-our-desire?p=1406467#post1406467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But that's just Adventure (or the Core even) with some setting restrictions.<br /> <br /> Maybe they can put out a &quot;Dark Eras&quot; type book for eras where only minor rule/theme adjustments are needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue that ANY period is just \u201cthis other TC Book with setting restrictions\u201d without some additional hook in there. I\u2019m confident that the 19th century is interesting enough to support and sustain games and that, if they did do a book for it, they\u2019ll come up with a better angle than just \u201cHere\u2019s the Victorian period, have fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it\u2019d be interesting to see what the setting is like before the Aeon Society existed. Though that kind of loses the easy justification for having a party that consisted of a Japanese Samurai, a Civil War Veteran, a Continental Opera Singer, a Gaucho, and an Opium Smuggler that the Aeon Society would provide at such a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T04:05:57-07:00","id":1406739,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking something along the lines of The Rowan series by Anne McCaffrey. Fleets of space ships on dozens of worlds all connected by a vast network of psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T10:33:54-07:00","id":1408185,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyones mentioned or heard of it, but there was once upon a time a project called Millenium's Edge - a far future, post Galactic Dark Times where the Aeon Institute is the equivalent to the Foundation. I'm wondering if any of the old notes are out there, because whoever started it got a good start on Psiads, Nova and alien templates, circa early 2000's. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm echoing the &quot;TNG&quot; Aeon option - what happens after the Doyen Wars, when human, Psion, Nova and Qin (and maybe Chromatics!) unite? And what biotech innovations are there for Joe Hologram to catch up? And what happens when humanity undergoes long term, deep space Tesser explorations - will the now-generational crews develop into some sort of new, telepathically connected group mind? <br /> <br /> Stuff like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25900-tritoninvestigator","name":"Tritoninvestigator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T11:10:47-07:00","id":1408188,"title":"","content":"Is it this one?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/additional_content/aeonsociety/2997/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/additional_content/aeonsociety/2997/\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.rpgpost.com/additional_content/aeonsociety/2997/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.rpgpost.com/additional_content/aeonsociety/2997/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Insp